# fixedbugs, defect 158, lane h158, 2026-10-02.
#
# Beside `fixedbugs-158-a-header-the-groups-header-includes-in-angle-brackets`:
# a macro defined twice, so clang's warning in the second header carries a
# note pointing back into the group's header, between that warning and the
# error. clang prints the error's stack again, and it is the one read.

extern "fixedbugs-158-noted-outer.h"
    function seven() -> i32  #~ ffi_missing_header

function main()
    print(seven())
